  "gb1168": {
    "id": "gb1168",
    "gregobaseId": "1168",
    "title": "Circumdederunt me",
    "part": "introit",
    "mode": "Introit · Septuagesima Sunday · Mode V",
    "gabc": "(c3) CIR(df~)CUM(f)DE(f)DÉ(f)RUNT(f_eef) me(d.) *(,) gé(fh)mi(f)tus(hh) mor(hi~)tis,(h.) (;) do(h)ló(hih)res(h_g) in(fe~)fér(fg~)ni(g.) (,) cir(gf~)cum(h_iH'//E)de(f!hgh)dé(fhee[ll:1]d)runt(d) me :(gxdf//egFD.1) (:) et(df) in(f) tri(fef)bu(f)la(f)ti(ef)ó(de'f)ne(f) me(fefd)a(d.) (;) in(d)vo(efe)cá(f!h'i)vi(hie'!f) Dó(fe)mi(h)num,(h_[oh:h]i_[oh:h]f.1_[oh:h]) (:) et(f) ex(hh)au(h)dí(hih)vit(h_g) (,) de(e) tem(fh~)plo(h) san(h)cto(gh) su(fheede)o(e[ll:1]d..) (;) vo(d!ewfefhhe'/f)cem(efe) me(de!fvED'e)am.(e[ll:1]d..) (::)",
    "latin": "Circumdedérunt me gémitus mortis, dolóres inférni circumdedérunt me : et in tribulatióne mea invocávi Dóminum, et exaudívit de templo sancto suo vocem meam.",
    "translation": "The groans of death surrounded me, the sorrows of hell encompassed me: and in my affliction I called upon the Lord, and he heard my voice from his holy temple.",
    "source": "Graduale Romanum (GregoBase #1168)",
    "usages": [
      {
        "calendar": "1962",
        "feastKey": "septuagesima",
        "part": "introit",
        "feastTitle": "Septuagesima Sunday",
        "rank": "Sunday"
      }
    ],
    "commentary": {
      "text": "Set as a polyphonic Introit by Heinrich Isaac in his Choralis Constantinus (Nuremberg, Formschneider, 1550). The same words are also shared with a responsory for the Office of the Dead, and in that guise were set by Hernando Franco — chapelmaster of Mexico City Cathedral (1575-85) — in what one modern study identifies as the first polyphonic composition for the dead written in early colonial America.",
      "source": "CPDL ChoralWiki, \"Circumdederunt me (Heinrich Isaac)\"; Javier Marín López, \"Hernando Franco's Circumdederunt me: The First Piece for the Dead in Early Colonial America.\""
    }
  },
